> And the 'normal' end of meditation for them is 'automatically when the 
> player character comes into sight'? Or is it a more complex issue?

Hostile monsters that are meditating pending your arrival will stop
meditating once they can see you and they get a turn, yes. That covers
Quest Nemeses, Vlad, Medusa, laired demons, and the Wizard.  Note that
of these, only the Wizard, the demons, the Minion of Huhetotl, the
Chromatic Dragon, Ixoth, Master Kaen, and Nalzok can see invisible.

Peaceful monsters will continue meditating until disturbed (Quest
Leaders and prisoners, though the latter will stop meditating once
they speak to you and the former won't), with "disturbed" including
any attack move including one that you decide not to follow through
with, or just being #chatted with. Any meditating monster will have
its meditation broken by losing HP, having stuff thrown at it, and
a few similar cases.

